-- title:
--   Tube annuli at a supersingular place, with discs and crossing models
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q\ge 5$, $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$; $k$ denotes the residue field of $A$. Write $F_C=$ `modularFunctionFieldC k M'` for the intermediate field of $k((\mathfrak q))$ generated by the $j$-series and its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion, $\bar F_0=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` for the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$, and $F=$ `fieldBar q M'` for the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, $H=$ `levelH q M'` being the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Places are taken in the sense of [`AlgebraicCurve.Place`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L22) (a proper valuation subring containing the base field, with principal ideals), with its order function `ord`, its rationality predicate `IsRational` (surjectivity of the base field into the residue field) and its evaluation `evalAt`. Below, $j$ denotes the element of $\bar F_0$ given by the coefficientwise image of the rational $q$-expansion `jq`, and also its image in $F$ under the inclusion given by `hle`; the phrase *$f$ is $j$-integral* abbreviates: $\mathrm{ord}_P(f)\ge 0$ at every place $P$ of $\bar F_0$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $\mathrm{ord}_P(j)\ge 0$.
--
--   The data are: a finite set $W$ of places of $F_C$ over $k$ with `hW` saying that $W$ is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' k` of supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in `ssJSet q k`); the inclusion `hle` of $\bar F_0$ in $F$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from $\bar F_0$ to $F_C$ (`ConstantReduction`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` lying over $A$, a surjective residue map onto $F_C$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with constants, with the scaling and divisor-pushforward axioms), together with `hR₀`, which requires that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\bar F_0$, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$; an index $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$); families of valuation subrings $O^{Ig}_\ell$ of $F$ indexed by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$, and $O^{SS}_{s'}$ indexed by $W$.
--
--   These subrings are pinned down by: `hIg_inf`, saying that $f\in O^{Ig}_{\infty}$ (for the point `lineInfty q`) if and only if $f\cdot y=x$ for some Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ of non-zero coefficientwise reduction; `hIg`, saying that for each $\ell$ there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ whose reduction `redQ q γ` carries $\infty$ to $\ell$ and with $O^{Ig}_\ell$ the pullback of $O^{Ig}_{\infty}$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; and `hSS`, which for each $s'\in W$ imposes four clauses on $O=O^{SS}_{s'}$: (i) $O$ lies over $A$, i.e. a constant lies in $O$ exactly when it lies in $A$; (ii) there is $t\in O$ such that $t-a$ lies in $O$ and is a unit there for every $a\in A$; (iii) for every $j$-integral $f\in$ `R₀.integers` whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s'$, the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in $O$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s'.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O$; (iv) $O$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   Further data: fields $F^{Ig}_\ell$ and $F^{SS}_{s'}$, each a $k$-algebra; component charts $C^{Ig}_\ell$ of $A$ on $F$ with values in $F^{Ig}_\ell$ (`ComponentChart`: integers, residue, a domain of places, a finite set of nodes, a place map, with the axioms of that structure) with `hCIg : (CIg ℓ).integers = OIg ℓ`; regular prolongations $R^{SS}_{s'}$ with values in $F^{SS}_{s'}$ and `hRSS : (RSS s').integers = OSS s'`; component charts $C^{SS}_{s'}$ with values in $F^{SS}_{s'}$ and `hCSS : (CSS s').integers = OSS s'`; places $x_{\ell,s'}$ of $F^{Ig}_\ell$ over $k$ with `hxs_mem` putting $x_{\ell,s'}$ in the node set of $C^{Ig}_\ell$, and `hxs_over`, which for each $\ell$ provides a ring homomorphism $\mathfrak j:F_C\to F^{Ig}_\ell$ such that every $f\in$ `R₀.integers` has image in $(C^{Ig}_\ell)$.integers with chart residue $\mathfrak j(R_0\text{-residue of }f)$, and such that for every $s'\in W$ and $g\in F_C$, $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s'$ precisely when $\mathfrak j(g)$ lies in that of $x_{\ell,s'}$. Finally $\pi_t\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfies $\pi_t^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi_t\in A$, and $s\in W$ is fixed.
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of two families of annuli $\mathrm{An},\mathrm{An}':\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)\to$ `Annulus A F` (each annulus consisting of a set `dom` of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a parameter `param` and a modulus in the maximal ideal of $A$, subject to the axioms of that structure: rationality and parameter conditions on the points of `dom`, unique representability of admissible values, $\mathrm{ord}_P(\mathrm{param}-P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,\mathrm{param})=1$, and the unit principle) and of a family of places $x'_\ell$ of $F^{SS}_s$ over $k$, written $xt$, such that the following hold.
--
--   (1) Stability of the family of $x'_\ell$ under semilinear automorphisms: for every $g\in$ `SemilinearAut` $(\overline{\mathbb Q},F)$ (a pair consisting of a ring automorphism of $F$ and one of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, compatible with the structure map) whose base automorphism preserves $A$ (a constant lies in $A$ if and only if its image does) and is congruent to the identity modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ on $A$, and which fixes $j$, and for every $\varphi\in\mathrm{Aut}_k(F^{SS}_s)$ such that $g$ preserves $(R^{SS}_s)$.integers and induces $\varphi$ on residues: a place $Q$ of $F^{SS}_s$ lies in the range of $xt$ if and only if $\varphi\cdot Q$ does.
--
--   (2) For each $\ell$: $\mathrm{An}'_\ell$ and $\mathrm{An}_\ell$ have the same domain and the same modulus; that modulus is non-zero in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and equals $u\pi_t^{w}$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ and some $w\ge 1$; for every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` with `A.tameCharacter πt τ = 1`, the semilinear automorphism $g$ of $F$ obtained from $\tau$ by the coefficientwise action [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M'))`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) satisfies: $P\in\mathrm{An}_\ell.\mathrm{dom}$ if and only if $g\cdot P\in\mathrm{An}_\ell.\mathrm{dom}$, and $g$ fixes both parameters; and the two parameters are reciprocal up to the modulus: $\mathrm{An}'_\ell.\mathrm{param}\cdot\mathrm{An}_\ell.\mathrm{param}$ equals the image in $F$ of the modulus.
--
--   (3) For each $\ell$: $\mathrm{An}_\ell$ is attached to $C^{Ig}_\ell$ at $x_{\ell,s}$ in the sense of `IsAttached`, namely $x_{\ell,s}$ is a node of the chart, the parameter lies in the chart's integers with $\mathrm{ord}_{x_{\ell,s}}$ of its residue equal to $1$, and for every $f$ in the chart's integers with non-zero residue and $\mathrm{ord}_P f=0$ at all $P\in\mathrm{An}_\ell.\mathrm{dom}$ one has, at each such $P$, that $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\cdot(P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,\mathrm{param})^{-\mathrm{ord}_{x_{\ell,s}}(\text{residue of }f)}$ lies in $A$ and is a unit there. The same attachment statement is made for $\mathrm{An}'_\ell$ against the regular prolongation $R^{SS}_s$ and the place $x'_\ell$, written out directly: the parameter of $\mathrm{An}'_\ell$ lies in $(R^{SS}_s)$.integers with $\mathrm{ord}_{x'_\ell}$ of its residue equal to $1$, and the corresponding unit law holds for every $f$ in $(R^{SS}_s)$.integers with non-zero residue which is a unit at all points of $\mathrm{An}'_\ell.\mathrm{dom}$.
--
--   (4) $xt$ is injective.
--
--   (5) The domains are pairwise disjoint: a place lying in $\mathrm{An}_\ell.\mathrm{dom}$ and in $\mathrm{An}_{\ell'}.\mathrm{dom}$ forces $\ell=\ell'$.
--
--   (6) Each domain lies in the supersingular tube of $s$: for every $\ell$, every $P\in\mathrm{An}_\ell.\mathrm{dom}$, every $j$-integral $f\in$ `R₀.integers` whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)-a$ lies in $A$ and in its maximal ideal.
--
--   (7) Equivariance for the level automorphisms: for all $\zeta'$, all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ such that the pullback of $O^{Ig}_\ell$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` is $O^{Ig}_{\sigma\ell}$ for all $\ell$, the pulled-back annulus $\mathrm{An}_\ell.\mathrm{comap}$ along that automorphism has domain $\mathrm{An}_{\sigma\ell}.\mathrm{dom}$, and $\mathrm{An}_\ell$ and $\mathrm{An}_{\sigma\ell}$ have the same modulus.
--
--   (8) A node-ring clause presenting the completions as crossing models. There exist: an index type $\Lambda$; subrings $C'_l$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, all contained in $A$, each a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with elements $\varpi'_l\in C'_l$; a base index $l_0$; rings $W_l$, each a complete discrete valuation domain (adically complete for its maximal ideal) with an element $\pi_l$; natural numbers $E_l$ and $E_0$; subrings $\mathcal N_\ell$ of $F$ and $\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$ of $F$, the latter equipped with local-ring and Noetherian witnesses; and functions $x,y,u$ from $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ to $F$, such that: the residue in $k$ of $d\in C'_l$ vanishes exactly when $d\in\varpi'_l C'_l$; $C'_{l_0}\subseteq C'_l$ for all $l$; $\varpi'_{l_0}\ne 0$; every element of $A$ is algebraic over $C'_{l_0}$; each $\pi_l$ is irreducible and $E_l\ge 1$; and for each $\ell$: $\mathrm{An}_\ell.\mathrm{param}=y_\ell$; the modulus of $\mathrm{An}_\ell$ equals $(\varpi'_{l_0})^{E_0}$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; $x_{\ell,s}$, $x'_\ell$ and all points of $\mathrm{An}_\ell.\mathrm{dom}$ are rational; $\mathcal N_\ell$ consists exactly of those $f\in F$ lying in $(C^{Ig}_\ell)$.integers, in $(R^{SS}_s)$.integers and in the valuation subring of every $P\in\mathrm{An}_\ell.\mathrm{dom}$; every $f\in\mathcal N_\ell$ has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$ at all such $P$; $x_\ell y_\ell$ is the image of $(\varpi'_{l_0})^{E_0}$ times $u_\ell$; if $x_\ell$ lies in the Igusa chart's integers its residue is $0$, if it lies in $(R^{SS}_s)$.integers then $\mathrm{ord}_{x'_\ell}$ of its residue is $1$; if $y_\ell$ lies in $(R^{SS}_s)$.integers its residue is $0$, and if it lies in the Igusa chart's integers then $\mathrm{ord}_{x_{\ell,s}}$ of its residue is $1$; every $f\in F$ is a fraction $a/b$ with $a,b\in\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$, $b\ne 0$, for some $l$, and also admits $b\ne 0$ in $\mathcal N_{\ell,l_0}$ with $fb$ a finite $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-linear combination of elements of $\mathcal N_{\ell,l_0}$. Moreover, for each $l$: $\mathcal N_{\ell,l_0}\subseteq\mathcal N_{\ell,l}\subseteq\mathcal N_\ell$; a place $P$ lies in $\mathrm{An}_\ell.\mathrm{dom}$ if and only if $\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$ is contained in its valuation subring and every non-unit $f$ of $\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$ has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ in the maximal ideal of $A$; the image of $C'_l$ lies in $\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$; every element of $\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$ differs from (the image of) some element of $C'_l$ by a non-unit; any family of elements of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $C'_l$ annihilates only the zero family of coefficients in $\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$; there is a subring $B\subseteq\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$ containing $x_\ell,y_\ell,u_\ell$ such that $\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$ is the set of $f$ with $fh=g$ for some $g,h\in B$ with $h$ a unit of $\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$, and such that $B$ is the subring generated by the image of $C'_l$ together with a finite set; $x_\ell,y_\ell\in\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$ and $u_\ell$ is a unit of $\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$; and there are a ring homomorphism $\sigma:W_l\to$ the adic completion of $\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$ at its maximal ideal and a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from that completion onto `UVCrossingModel` $(W_l,\pi_l^{E_l})$, that is $W_l[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_l^{E_l})$, such that $\sigma(\pi_l)$ is the image of $\varpi'_l$ whenever the latter lies in $\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$, $\iota(\sigma(o))=\mathrm{const}(o)$ for all $o\in W_l$, every element of $C'_l$ whose image lies in $\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$ is in the image of $\sigma$, and the two order–monomial laws hold: for $f\in\mathcal N_{\ell,l}$ lying in the Igusa chart's integers with non-zero residue of order $n$ at $x_{\ell,s}$ there is a unit $\gamma$ of the crossing model with $\iota(f)-\gamma V^n$ in the ideal generated by $\mathrm{const}(\pi_l)$ and $U$, and symmetrically, for $f$ in $(R^{SS}_s)$.integers with non-zero residue of order $n$ at $x'_\ell$, a unit $\gamma$ with $\iota(f)-\gamma U^n$ in the ideal generated by $\mathrm{const}(\pi_l)$ and $V$.
--
--   (9) A moduli normalisation clause: there are $J\in F$ whose Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) and a constant $a_0\in A$ such that $J-a_0$ lies in $(R^{SS}_s)$.integers with residue $0$, the residue of $a_0$ satisfies $\bar a_0^{\,q}=s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\,$`jGeomGen k M'`$)$, and there is $c'\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $c'(J-a_0)$ in $(R^{SS}_s)$.integers of non-zero residue such that for every $\ell$ the element $J-a_0$ lies in $(C^{Ig}_\ell)$.integers with non-zero residue and $\mathrm{ord}_{x'_\ell}$ of the residue of $c'(J-a_0)$ equals minus $\mathrm{ord}_{x_{\ell,s}}$ of the residue of $J-a_0$ on the Igusa chart.
--
--   (10) Finally, there exist $\mathrm{disc}$, assigning to each place $Q$ of $F^{SS}_s$ over $k$ a set of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $\mathrm{coord}$, assigning to each such $Q$ an element of $F$, such that: $(R^{SS}_s).\mathrm{DiscFamily}$ holds for the finite set `Finset.univ.image xt` with these data, i.e. for every $Q$ outside the range of $xt$ the pair $(\mathrm{disc}\,Q,\mathrm{coord}\,Q)$ is a residue disc (the conjunction of `IsDiscCoord`, `PointwiseOn` and `DegreeOn`), and two such $Q$ with a common point in their discs coincide; for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}(F)$ generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $(R^{SS}_s)$.integers, the induced residue automorphism `(RSS s).resAut τ` stabilises the range of $xt$, and for $Q$ outside that range it carries discs to discs, $\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau(\mathrm{disc}\,Q)=\mathrm{disc}((R^{SS}_s).\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q)$; for every $\ell$, no point of $\mathrm{An}'_\ell.\mathrm{dom}$ lies in a disc of a $Q$ outside the range of $xt$; for every semilinear $g$ as in (1) (preserving $A$, congruent to the identity modulo the maximal ideal, fixing $j$) inducing $\varphi$ on the residue field and such that $\varphi$ stabilises the range of $xt$, and for every $Q$ outside that range, a place $P$ lies in $\mathrm{disc}\,Q$ if and only if $g\cdot P$ lies in $\mathrm{disc}(\varphi\cdot Q)$; for $Q$ outside the range of $xt$, every $P\in\mathrm{disc}\,Q$ satisfies $\mathrm{ord}_P(j)\ge 0$; and, covering the tube, every rational place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying the tube condition of (6) (for every $j$-integral $f\in$ `R₀.integers` with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$ and every $a\in A$ with residue $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)-a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$) either lies in $\mathrm{disc}\,Q$ for some $Q$ outside the range of $xt$, or lies in $\mathrm{An}'_\ell.\mathrm{dom}$ for some $\ell$.
--
--   This is the local analysis of the stable reduction of the modular curve $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ at a supersingular point in characteristic $q$: at a fixed supersingular place $s$ the $q+1$ tubes are produced as two-ended annuli, attached at one end to the Igusa components and at the other to the supersingular (Drinfeld) component, together with the residue discs of the latter, the crossing-model presentations of the node rings, and the normalisation of the moduli $j$-invariant. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted) in assembling a semistable covering of the curve.
